# Odoo.sh Staging Environment

**Effective:** 2026-03-31

## Staging instance

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| URL | `https://cryptoxdog-ib-odoo-19-staging-30217068.dev.odoo.com` |
| Build ID | `30217068` |
| Branch | `Staging` |
| Platform | Odoo.sh |

## SSH access

```bash
ssh 30217068@cryptoxdog-ib-odoo-19-staging-30217068.dev.odoo.com
```

- The build number is the SSH username.
- The host is the full Odoo.sh development domain.
- The operator's SSH key must be registered in project settings.
- Confirm the current build in Odoo.sh before relying on this reference; build IDs rotate.

## Shell commands

```bash
# Odoo shell
odoo-bin shell -d <dbname>

# Logs
cat ~/logs/odoo.log
tail -f ~/logs/odoo.log

# Update a module
odoo-bin -u plasticos_base --stop-after-init

# Install a module
odoo-bin -i plasticos_new_module --stop-after-init
```

## Web lead staging endpoints

| Method | Path | Auth |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/api/v1/web-lead` | Bearer token |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/cognito-webhook` | Bearer token |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/web-lead/health` | None |

## Deployment boundary

- A push to `Staging` triggers an Odoo.sh deployment.
- Commit and push both require explicit operator authorization.
- SSH sessions are ephemeral; changes outside persistent storage are lost on rebuild.
- Confirm the database name from the Odoo.sh dashboard or shell before running commands.
